TITLE:: MultiF0Tracker
summary:: A multi-pitch tracking engine for complex polyphonic audio.
categories:: Analysis, Pitch
related:: Classes/AffordanceField, Classes/VoiceTrack

DESCRIPTION::
MultiF0Tracker is a robust engine designed to track multiple concurrent pitches (F0s) in a real-time or batch audio stream. It is specifically optimized for vocal ensembles (A Cappella) and complex acoustic environments.

The tracker employs a "Detect and Match" strategy:
1. It computes a strong::Salience Function:: across a logarithmic frequency scale, using harmonic summation to highlight potential fundamental frequencies.
2. It detects peaks in the salience function.
3. It manages a collection of strong::VoiceTrack:: objects, representing active melodic lines.
4. It uses a distance-based assignment logic (simplified Hungarian algorithm) to associate new detections with existing tracks.

The tracker also includes logic for "Ghost" pitch detection and combination tone suppression, ensuring that overtones and intermodulation products are not misidentified as independent voices.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Create a new MultiF0Tracker.

ARGUMENT:: config
An optional instance of TrackerConfig. If nil, default settings are used.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: computeSalience
Calculate the F0 salience function for a given spectrum.

ARGUMENT:: spectrum
The magnitude spectrum.

ARGUMENT:: freqs
An array of frequencies corresponding to the spectrum bins.

RETURNS:: An array [f0Candidates, salience].

METHOD:: updateTracks
Update the internal state of voice tracks based on new pitch detections.

ARGUMENT:: detectedPitches
An array of [frequency, confidence] pairs.

ARGUMENT:: frame
The current frame index.

RETURNS:: An array of "sung" pitches (pitches currently associated with active tracks).

EXAMPLES::

code::
// Tracking a simulated moving pitch
c = TrackerConfig.new;
t = MultiF0Tracker.new(c);

// Frame 1
p1 = [[440, 0.9], [660, 0.7]];
t.updateTracks(p1, 0);

// Frame 2 (pitch shifts slightly)
p2 = [[442, 0.9], [663, 0.7]];
t.updateTracks(p2, 1);

t.tracks.do { |tr| postln("Track " + tr.id + " pitch: " + tr.lastPitch) };
::

THEORETICAL BACKGROUND::
Pitch tracking in polyphonic contexts is a "Grand Challenge" in Music Information Retrieval (MIR). MultiF0Tracker addresses this by combining bottom-up signal evidence (harmonic salience) with top-down temporal constraints (track persistence and jump limits).

The salience calculation uses the following weighted summation:
formula::
S(f0) = \sum_{h=1}^{H} W(h) \cdot M(f0 \cdot h)
::
Where W(h) is the weight of the h-th harmonic and M is the magnitude at that frequency.